Since you have more wishes than you know what to do with, I would advise 
you should wish for your Ring of Free Action right away. Levitation can 
wait, but without Free Action you're vulnerable to instant death if you 
happen to get a bit of bad luck with a gelatinous cube or something like 
that.

So, I reckon you should get that ring right away, and maybe upgrade your 
gloves.

If you're not going to polypile anything, then wishing for a t-shirt is 
probably a decent option, and then spending that magic marker writing 
enchant armour scrolls for all your end-game armour.

I usually don't wish for a helm of opposite alignment until I'm standing 
on the (wrong) high altar.

When I've got spare wishes, I often wish for a blessed figurine of 
Archon. It's not always a wise idea, but I find it fun. :)  (and if it 
ever dies, you might be able to grab it's shield of reflection.)

